 "meta": {
  "purpose": "English for the individual word tiles in the Sentence Builder, so tapping a word in translation mode shows what it means.",
  "why": "The decks gloss headwords, and a tile carries whatever form the sentence used — 'hu', 'liese', 'Bicher', 'd'Kanner'. Joining on the surface spelling reaches about half of them, and for a handful it reaches the wrong entry: the lexicon and the vocab deck both gloss the spelling 'de' as 'you', because it is also a clitic of 'du', while in nearly every sentence here it is the masculine article. These entries override that lookup and fill its gaps.",
  "rule": "English only. Not one Luxembourgish word is authored here — every key is a form that already occurs in a shipped sentence, and pipeline/test/sentences.test.js fails on any key that does not.",
  "ambiguity": "A form with more than one common reading is glossed with both, separated by ' / ', the way a dictionary does. A gloss that silently picks one reading is the failure this file exists to fix.",
  "addedAt": "2026-09-11"
 },
